#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Withdrawals finalise themselves: transfer webhooks + automatic Paystack check.

Why: Paystack sends ALL events to your one webhook URL (the deposits handler),
which ignored transfer events, so withdrawals and rider payouts stayed
"processing" forever and customers' money stayed on hold.

- The Paystack webhook now passes transfer.success / failed / reversed to the
  payouts app (success -> completed, failed -> refunded to the wallet).
- Safety net: every queue run (cron-job.org / process_withdrawal_queue) asks
  Paystack about transfers still "processing" and finalises them, including
  "abandoned" ones (refunded).
- Transfers waiting for a Paystack OTP: staff get an email (at most hourly).
- Customers are notified when a transfer fails and their money is refunded.

Unzip in the backend root (with manage.py), then:
    python3 apply_payout_sync_backend.py
    python manage.py test apps.payouts apps.payments --settings=config.settings.test
No migrations.
"""
